1
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:08,790
(Sheldon:)Would you like to play
a physics car game I invented

2
00:00:08,787 --> 00:00:10,657
called "I Can't Spy"?

3
00:00:11,789 --> 00:00:14,129
(Sheldon:)It's all the nail-biting
tension of "I Spy"

4
00:00:14,126 --> 00:00:17,126
(Sheldon:)but the added fun of subatomic
particles and waves

5
00:00:17,129 --> 00:00:19,229
(Sheldon:)outside the visible
spectrum.

6
00:00:19,231 --> 00:00:20,901
(Leonard:)If it's half as much fun as

7
00:00:20,899 --> 00:00:22,899
"One Times Ten to the Fourth
Bottles of Beer on the Wall,"

8
00:00:22,901 --> 00:00:24,571
(Leonard:)I'm in.

9
00:00:24,569 --> 00:00:26,239
(Sheldon:)I'll begin.

10
00:00:26,238 --> 00:00:30,638
(Sheldon:)Uh, I can't spy
with my little eye...

11
00:00:31,909 --> 00:00:34,609
(Sheldon:)...something passing
right through us.

12
00:00:34,613 --> 00:00:36,283
(Leonard:)That soy Frappuccino I had.

13
00:00:36,281 --> 00:00:37,411
(chuckles)

14
00:00:37,415 --> 00:00:39,245
(Sheldon:)Will you please
play the game?

15
00:00:39,251 --> 00:00:41,881
(Sheldon:)I can't spy
with my little eye

16
00:00:41,887 --> 00:00:43,887
(Sheldon:)something passing
right through us.

17
00:00:43,889 --> 00:00:46,059
(Leonard:)I don't know, um...

18
00:00:46,057 --> 00:00:48,727
(Leonard:)If 65 billion
solar neutrinos pass

19
00:00:48,727 --> 00:00:50,797
through a square centimeter
every second,

20
00:00:50,795 --> 00:00:52,795
(Leonard:)given the surface
area of this car is

21
00:00:52,797 --> 00:00:54,697
(Leonard:)about 60,000
square centimeters,

22
00:00:54,699 --> 00:01:01,019
(Leonard:)that means 3.9 times ten
to the 15th solar neutrinos?

